@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: deploy animation and death animation are LAYERS that compose, not two clips that replace each other
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no deploy, death, or animation-layer types exist
'   under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning
'   renderer before a covers: line can be honest.
'   rules that must not wait on the clip _spec/_plans/pawn-first-phase-gas-move.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "deploy animation x death animation layers" is a COMPOSITING change. The "x"
' is the stack, not a multiply in the rules: a unit can be entering the board
' and leaving it in one window, and both clips have to draw.
'
' Typical fail: death replaces deploy, or deploy wins and the corpse never
' plays. The player sees the wrong last frame, then mistrusts the rules.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   z-order (death above deploy, or the reverse)
'   whether a skipped animation is still a legal move
'   pooling, atlas, or a second canvas
'   whether tutorial playback uses the same stack
'
' Animation is not a rules lock. If a clip is late, the engine has already
' resolved the square. This plan must not introduce a wait that desyncs that.
title PLANNED — deploy and death are layers;\nneither clip may replace the other

component "rules resolve the square" as RULE <<app>>
component "deploy layer" as DEP <<app>>
component "death layer" as DIE <<app>>
component "**one clip wins**\nthe other frame is dropped" as DROP <<error>>
component "stacked layers\nboth clips draw" as STACK <<app>>
component "the player's last frame" as EYE <<app>>

RULE ARROW_MAIN DEP
RULE ARROW_MAIN DIE
DEP ARROW_ERROR DROP : current fail, if exclusive
DIE ARROW_ERROR DROP
DEP ARROW_OPTIONAL STACK
DIE ARROW_OPTIONAL STACK
STACK ARROW_MAIN EYE
DROP ARROW_ERROR EYE : the rules were right;\nthe picture lied

note bottom of DROP
  **Replacement is the defect because death
  unloading deploy leaves a blank when a unit dies
  on entry.** The composite stack has to retain
  both clips until each animation finishes
  independently.
end note

note bottom of STACK
  **Layers are required rather than a concatenated
  clip that delays death until deploy completes.**
  Draw both animations on the same tick and let
  each clock finish independently.
end note

note right of RULE
  **Rules resolution never awaits animation
  frames, because the square is settled before
  either clip starts.** A skipped animation
  remains a legal move, or the networked match
  falls out of sync.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Inventory the two clips.** Find the deploy player and the death player,
  and whether a unit can be in both states in one frame (entry-kill, swap,
  capture on drop). That overlap is the case this plan exists for.
  --
  **2. Put them on two layers.** Same unit, same tick, both draw. Pick a z-order
  and pin it with a screenshot test, not a comment.
  ==
  **3. Keep the engine off the clock.** Completing a move must not await
  onAnimationEnd. Reduced-motion and headless tests skip the stack and still
  pass the rules.
  --
  **Left open**: z-order; whether a third layer (hit spark, gas) joins this
  stack or a later one.
end legend
@enduml
